 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The basic sentence: A は B です",
     "texto": [
      "Almost everything you say at the start follows this pattern: **A は B です** (A is B).",
      "**は** is the particle that marks **what you are talking about** (the topic). Here it is read **wa**.",
      "**です** means «to be»: it always goes at the end and **does not change** with the person. It is pronounced «des», almost without the u.",
      "**わたし は アンナ です** = I am Anna. Word by word: «I — as for — Anna — am»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Phrases for introducing yourself",
     "texto": [
      "**はじめまして** is said the first time you meet someone.",
      "When you finish introducing yourself: **よろしく おねがいします** (literally «please treat me well»). It is essential.",
      "For other people, **さん** is added after the name: **たなか さん** (Mr or Mrs Tanaka). **Never** add it to your own name.",
      "To say nationality, **じん** is added to the country name: スペイン → **スペインじん** (Spanish), にほん → **にほんじん** (Japanese)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Where you come from",
     "texto": [
      "**スペイン から きました** = I come from Spain. **から** is the particle «from».",
      "To ask someone's name politely: **おなまえ は？** (your name?)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
